  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LIVELIHOOD RESTORATION SUPPORT TO WOMEN DISPLACED BY FLOOD AND FARMERS HERDERS CONFLICT IN VULNERABLE COMMUNITIES OF APA AND OTUKPO LGAS OF  BENUE STA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Livelihood Restoration Support to Women Displaced by Flood and Farmers Herders Conflict in Vulnerable Communities of Apa and Otukpo LGAs of  Benue state (LIVE &#x2013; RESWOD) is an intervention for building the resilience of vulnerable women in flood and conflict affected women and households through the provision of dignity kits, gender and conflict sensitivity training, and alternative income generating activities (IGA). The project will leverage on existing early warning mechanism established by the 6 project communities and government to enable members avoid and escape emergency situation.</narrative>
  </description>
